T*
() Tj
T*
(By the Trillion Man Outreach kitchen crew Updated October 8, 2026) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If dinner at your house comes with negotiations, you are in very large company. Picky) Tj
T*
(eating is common in kids, and the goal is not to win a standoff but to make meals calmer) Tj
T*
(and give children plenty of chances to get comfortable with new foods. Here are) Tj
T*
(strategies and dinners that help.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Five strategies that lower the pressure) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Serve it deconstructed.) Tj
T*
(Keep foods separate so kids can build their own plate. Tacos, baked potatoes and pasta) Tj
T*
(bars work well.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Keep one safe food on the table.) Tj
T*
(Bread, rice, fruit or plain pasta means nobody leaves hungry.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Offer, do not push.) Tj
T*
(Place new foods on the table without pressure. Kids often need many exposures before) Tj
T*
(they accept something.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let them help.) Tj
T*
(Stirring, sprinkling and naming a dish makes children more curious about eating it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Eat together when you can,) Tj
T*
(and let them see you enjoying the food.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Dinners that are easy to customize) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Baked potato bar) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Microwave or bake potatoes and set out cheese, black beans, broccoli, sour cream and) Tj
T*
(salsa. Each person tops their own. Our) Tj
T*
(microwave sweet potato with black beans) Tj
T*
(works the same way.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Taco night) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Salsa chicken, seasoned beans or ground meat, tortillas and a row of toppings. See) Tj
T*
(slow cooker dinners) Tj
T*
(for an easy base. Cook ground meat to 160 F.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pasta bar) Tj
T*
